  "term": "articulator",
  "definition": "In this historical source, articulator refers to the speech-articulating apparatus or to disorders of articulation rather than disorders of word choice or language. Such disturbances include unclear or mumbled speech, stammering or stuttering-like interruptions, repeated syllables, and shaky utterance.",
